            <ArticleTitle>A Nonlethal Case of Junctional Epidermolysis Bullosa and Congenital Pyloric Atresia: Compound Heterozygosity in a Patient with a Novel Integrin Beta 4 Gene Mutation.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-3476(17)31242-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpeds.2017.09.023</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of nonfatal junctional epidermolysis bullosa and pyloric atresia in a newborn. We identified a substitution (c.914C&gt;T) for the integrin β4 gene that has been associated with favorable outcome. A novel mutation (c.2011T&gt;G) of unknown significance was also found in this patient who is now thriving.</AbstractText>
